Give away her gowns,
 Give away her shoes;
 She has no more use
 For her fragrant gowns;
 Take them all down,
 Blue, green, blue,
 Lilac, pink, blue,
 From their padded hangers;
 She will dance no more
 In her narrow shoes;
 Sweep her narrow shoes
 From the closet floor.

